== 5.8 Chapter 5 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Advertising is best defined as],
  [a free mention in a newspaper],
  [a salesman's talk],
  [paid non-personal communication by an identified sponsor],
  [any news about a product]
)

#mcq(2, [Publicity differs from advertising because publicity is],
  [unpaid],
  [paid for],
  [personal],
  [illegal]
)

#mcq(3, [Personal selling differs from advertising because personal selling is],
  [free],
  [face to face],
  [paid],
  [non-personal]
)

#mcq(4, [The four stages of AIDA are],
  [attention, interest, desire, action],
  [appeal, interest, design, advertising],
  [attention, income, demand, action],
  [advertising, interest, demand, approval]
)

#mcq(5, [An advertisement that tells the market a new product exists is],
  [informative],
  [institutional],
  [reminder],
  [persuasive]
)

#mcq(6, [An advertisement that keeps an established brand familiar is],
  [public service],
  [informative],
  [reminder],
  [persuasive]
)

#mcq(7, [Advertising that promotes a whole class of product rather than one brand is],
  [selective],
  [primary or generic],
  [comparative],
  [institutional]
)

#mcq(8, [An advertisement paid for by a maker to promote its own brand is],
  [generic],
  [public service],
  [institutional],
  [selective]
)

#mcq(9, [Advertising designed to build the reputation of the firm rather than sell a product is],
  [generic],
  [reminder],
  [institutional],
  [selective]
)

#mcq(10, [A campaign urging citizens to pay their taxes is],
  [reminder advertising],
  [public service advertising],
  [institutional advertising],
  [selective advertising]
)

#mcq(11, [The medium that offers sight, sound and mass reach is],
  [television],
  [newspaper],
  [radio],
  [poster]
)

#mcq(12, [The medium best suited to a local trader with a small budget is],
  [television],
  [a national newspaper],
  [cinema],
  [radio]
)

#mcq(13, [The medium that gives the longest life to a detailed message is],
  [television],
  [radio],
  [poster],
  [magazine]
)

#mcq(14, [Direct mail is most suitable when],
  [the seller has a named list of likely buyers],
  [the message must reach everyone],
  [the budget is unlimited],
  [the product is cheap and universal]
)

#mcq(15, [A roadside poster is limited mainly by],
  [cost],
  [colour],
  [reach],
  [the length of the message it can carry]
)

#mcq(16, [Which is an advantage of internet advertising?],
  [it cannot be measured],
  [it reaches only young people],
  [it is always free],
  [it can be targeted and its response measured]
)

#mcq(17, [Sales promotion is best described as],
  [long-term brand building],
  [personal selling],
  [a short-term inducement to buy],
  [a form of publicity]
)

#mcq(18, [A voucher entitling the holder to money off the next purchase is a],
  [loyalty scheme],
  [coupon],
  [premium],
  [trade-in]
)

#mcq(19, [Offering a free plastic bowl with three bars of soap is a],
  [competition],
  [coupon],
  [price cut],
  [premium offer]
)

#mcq(20, [A manufacturer accepting an old machine against the price of a new one is offering a],
  [free sample],
  [trade-in],
  [loyalty card],
  [coupon]
)

#mcq(21, [Point-of-sale display is effective because it],
  [reaches people at the moment of purchase],
  [builds long-term loyalty],
  [is cheap on television],
  [replaces the product]
)

#mcq(22, [A free sample is used mainly when],
  [the market is small],
  [the price is high],
  [the brand is already famous],
  [the product is new and must be tried]
)

#mcq(23, [Which is NOT a form of sales promotion?],
  [price reduction],
  [television news coverage],
  [competition],
  [free sample]
)

#mcq(24, [Sales promotion differs from advertising because promotion],
  [is always free],
  [is non-personal],
  [offers an extra reason to buy now],
  [creates awareness]
)

#mcq(25, [A brand is],
  [a packaging material],
  [a legal right],
  [a price],
  [a name or symbol that identifies a seller's goods]
)

#mcq(26, [The legal protection for a brand name is a],
  [copyright],
  [licence],
  [trademark],
  [patent]
)

#mcq(27, [Packaging performs all these functions EXCEPT],
  [identifying the brand],
  [promoting the sale],
  [manufacturing the goods],
  [protecting the goods]
)

#mcq(28, [Which is an advantage of branding to the consumer?],
  [a guarantee of consistent quality],
  [more advertising],
  [higher prices],
  [less choice]
)

#mcq(29, [Which is an advantage of branding to the seller?],
  [it supports a higher price and repeat purchase],
  [it lowers the cost of production],
  [it removes competition],
  [it removes the need to advertise]
)

#mcq(30, [Advertising is criticised for],
  [improving quality],
  [informing buyers],
  [creating wants and raising costs],
  [reducing prices]
)

#mcq(31, [Advertising can raise the price of a product because],
  [its cost is added to the selling price],
  [it reduces demand],
  [it reduces competition],
  [it is illegal]
)

#mcq(32, [Advertising can lower the price of a product in the long run because],
  [it removes competition],
  [it reduces quality],
  [it is free],
  [it increases demand and allows economies of scale]
)

#mcq(33, [A firm selling industrial chemicals to five factories should advertise in],
  [a cinema],
  [a trade journal],
  [a national newspaper],
  [television]
)

#mcq(34, [The message of an advertisement is decided by],
  [the government],
  [the printer],
  [the medium],
  [the target market and the purpose]
)

#mcq(35, [Advertising that compares a brand directly with a named rival is],
  [generic],
  [institutional],
  [comparative],
  [reminder]
)

#mcq(36, [A loyalty scheme rewards],
  [complaints],
  [new customers only],
  [staff],
  [repeat purchase]
)

#mcq(37, [Which statement about advertising is correct?],
  [it creates awareness and preference, not a sale by itself],
  [it guarantees sales],
  [it replaces the product],
  [it is always wasted]
)

#mcq(38, [The Advertising Practitioners Council of Nigeria regulates],
  [banking],
  [advertising practice and content],
  [product quality],
  [insurance]
)

#mcq(39, [Advertising to children is restricted because],
  [it is cheap],
  [children have no money],
  [children cannot judge the claims],
  [it is illegal to advertise]
)

#mcq(40, [The most suitable medium for a new bank opening a branch in a town is],
  [direct mail to the whole country],
  [international television],
  [a trade magazine],
  [local radio and posters]
)

